# The pre-push hook runs under sh, which refuses CRLF line endings. With the
# machine's core.autocrlf=true a plain checkout would rewrite it and silently
# stop the gate from firing.
.githooks/pre-push text eol=lf

# Story 2.8 (spec review pass 1 E2, corrected by pass 2 P2-8): the venue
# generator's --check compares the committed 00016 against its own render, and
# with core.autocrlf=true a CRLF worktree used to make that compare red at line
# 1 on a fresh clone. The real mitigation is `normalizeEol` in
# supabase/scripts/pipeline/venueBackfill.ts, applied on BOTH sides of both
# compares, so this pin is hygiene rather than the fix — and note what it costs:
# the pattern covers every file in supabase/migrations/, and attributes bind at
# checkout, so `git ls-files --eol` still reports the pre-2.8 migrations as
# w/crlf until someone renormalizes (that renormalize will show as whole-file
# EOL churn in 14 migrations this story never touches). The two data CSVs are
# listed because they are the generator's and the probe's input vocabulary.
supabase/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
supabase/scripts/pipeline/data/game7_venues_curated.csv text eol=lf
supabase/scripts/pipeline/data/game7_feed_aliases.csv text eol=lf
# Story 6.9: the ABA Game 7 venue file is Story 6.10's generator input, pinned for the same reason.
supabase/scripts/pipeline/data/aba_game7_venues.csv text eol=lf
# Story 6.11: the 1968 ABA Finals game file is 00021's input, pinned for the same reason.
supabase/scripts/pipeline/data/aba_1968_finals.csv text eol=lf
